# Flutter Architecture Rules

## Recommended layers
Use clear separation between:
- Presentation/UI.
- Application/state orchestration.
- Domain models/use-case-facing interfaces where justified.
- Data repositories.
- Remote data sources.
- Local data sources.
- Sync/offline infrastructure.
- External integrations such as maps and notifications.

## Rules
- UI widgets MUST NOT contain API calls, SQL, or complex domain workflows.
- Screens should communicate through state/application controllers/view models consistent with the chosen state-management approach.
- Repositories coordinate local/remote sources and hide persistence details from the UI.
- Remote and local data models may be distinct when necessary; do not force network DTOs to become UI state.
- External provider SDKs should be isolated behind app services/interfaces where practical.
- Keep navigation decisions separate from data persistence.
- Organize features around product domains rather than generic utility folders when the feature is substantial.
